  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "In a Cartesian coordinate system in the plane, point \\(P(4,3)\\) is rotated \\(90^\\circ\\) counterclockwise about point \\(C(1,1)\\) to obtain point \\(P'\\). Find the coordinates of \\(P'\\) (enter the x-coordinate followed by the y-coordinate, separated by a comma).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "-1，4",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Relative to \\(C(1,1)\\), \\(P(4,3)\\) is \\(4-1=3\\) units right and \\(3-1=2\\) units up. A \\(90^\\circ\\) counterclockwise rotation turns a rightward step upward and an upward step leftward, preserving their lengths. Thus \\(P'\\) is \\(2\\) units left and \\(3\\) units up from \\(C\\), giving\n\\[\nP'=(1-2,\\,1+3)=(-1,4).\n\\]",
